Softmax is invariant to adding a constant to every logit, which is why
stable implementations subtract max(logit) before exp to avoid overflow.

Why the logit gradient is p - y:
  CE loss  L = -log p_c where p = softmax(z)
  dL/dz_k = p_k - 1[k == c] = p_k - y_k   (y one-hot)
This simple form is the whole reason softmax is paired with cross-entropy.

